---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How this site handles contact information, technical request data and third-party media."
  updated="2026-09-02"
>
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    This is the personal portfolio of Patrick Barnhardt. It does not carry
    advertising or advertising trackers. It does measure traffic, using Google
    Analytics, as described below. Patrick does not sell or rent personal
    information he receives through the site; he uses it only to operate the
    site, protect the contact form, understand which pages are read and
    respond to messages.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you provide</h2>
  <p>
    The contact form requires a name, email address and message. Depending on
    the type of inquiry, it may also accept a company or studio name, telephone
    number, subject, project link, timing and other project details. Those
    optional fields are used only to understand and respond to the inquiry.
  </p>
  <p>
    A submission is delivered as email to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    The site does not keep a separate database of contact submissions. The
    contact service records limited delivery and diagnostic information, such
    as a submission identifier, inquiry type, delivery identifier and request
    identifier, but does not write the submitted form fields or message body to
    its application logs.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and anti-spam protection</h2>
  <p>
    The public site is hosted through GitHub Pages. GitHub may process
    technical request information as described in its{' '}
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">privacy statement</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The home page loads Cloudflare Turnstile to protect the contact form from
    automated abuse. Turnstile processes technical signals including IP
    address, user-agent information, TLS fingerprint, site key and the site's
    origin. The form's server-side verification also sends the connecting IP
    address to Cloudflare. Cloudflare explains this processing in its{' '}
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Every page loads Google Analytics 4, which counts visits and records which
    pages are read. The tag sets first-party cookies in your browser and sends
    Google the page address, the referring page, general device and browser
    information and an approximate location derived from your IP address.
    Google states that Analytics does not log or store full IP addresses.
  </p>
  <p>
    Patrick sees only aggregate reports — page counts, referrers, countries —
    and uses them to decide which work is worth keeping current. The property
    has no advertising features enabled, and the data is not used to target
    ads to you or sold to anyone. Google's own handling is described in its{' '}
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>{' '}
    and in{' '}
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Embedded and externally hosted media</h2>
  <p>
    Some portfolio thumbnails are served by YouTube. Certain project pages and
    media viewers also include videos from YouTube's privacy-enhanced domain or
    interactive models from Sketchfab. When that media is requested, the
    provider receives normal browser and network request information and may
    process it under its own privacy policy. You can avoid loading an
    interactive embed by not opening that media or visiting its project page.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google and YouTube privacy policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://sketchfab.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Sketchfab privacy policy</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long information is kept</h2>
  <p>
    Contact email is retained only as long as reasonably necessary to answer
    the inquiry, maintain records of a potential or completed working
    relationship, resolve disputes or meet legal obligations. Infrastructure
    and security providers retain their own operational records according to
    their respective policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You may contact Patrick directly by email instead of using the form. To ask
    what personal information from a contact submission is held, request a
    correction or request deletion where applicable, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    To stay out of the analytics counts, block cookies or scripts for this site
    in your browser, or install Google's{' '}
    <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    Nothing on the site requires analytics to work, and blocking it will not
    break any page.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    This notice will be updated when the site's data practices or service
    providers materially change. The date above identifies the current version.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
